From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server, ntdll, kernelbase: a process keeps the mitigation and child process policies it is created with

CreateProcess dropped PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_POLICY and
PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_CHILD_PROCESS_POLICY ("Unsupported attribute", the
most frequent CreateProcessInternalW fixme: Chromium and Edge start every
sandboxed process with them), so the child reported no mitigation
policies, and a renderer told to create no processes could create them.
The component filter and mitigation audit attributes were also reported
as unsupported.

- NtCreateUserProcess takes PS_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_OPTIONS (one to three
  64-bit masks) and PS_ATTRIBUTE_CHILD_PROCESS_POLICY, and the server keeps
  them with the process (new_process's creation policy).
- A process created with PROCESS_CREATION_CHILD_PROCESS_RESTRICTED (or
  RESTRICTED_UNLESS_SECURE: there are no secure processes here), or that
  set NoChildProcessCreation on itself with SetProcessMitigationPolicy,
  creates no process: STATUS_CHILD_PROCESS_BLOCKED,
  ERROR_CHILD_PROCESS_BLOCKED. A restriction is never lifted.
- GetProcessMitigationPolicy reports the policies a process was created
  with (ASLR, dynamic code, strict handle checks, system call disable,
  extension points, signatures, fonts, image loads, child processes), for
  itself and for another process (new request
  get_process_creation_policy); a policy set at creation cannot be turned
  off by SetProcessMitigationPolicy.
- The component filter (which only keeps KTM from a process) and the audit
  policy are accepted; PROTECTION_LEVEL_SAME from an unprotected process
  is no protection; the desktop app policy concerns packaged processes.
- winbase.h: the PROCESS_CREATION_CHILD_PROCESS_*,
  PROCESS_CREATION_DESKTOP_APP_BREAKAWAY_* and
  PROCESS_CREATION_MITIGATION_POLICY(2)_* values.

Protocol change: SERVER_PROTOCOL_VERSION 868 (a full rebuild).

Wine's kernel32 process tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/childpolicy-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit: a child started with the
policies reports them and is refused a process; the parent reads them; a
process restricts itself; the extra attributes are accepted). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_CHILD_PROCESSES_ALLOWED (server/process.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_CREATION_POLICY (ntdll/unix/process.c),
SG_MUTANT_NO_CREATION_ATTRS (kernelbase/process.c).
